If $a,b,c$ are all distinct, then $\mu a = \mu b = \mu c = 1$, forcing $a=b=c$, a contradiction. Hence at the extremum, **two variables are equal**. (The boundary $v=0$ is handled below.) Since $F$ is increasing in $u$, the global minimum of $F$ is achieved when two variables are equal.

